    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Evaporation rate increases with higher surface area, elevated temperature, and increased wind speed, but decreases with higher humidity.",
        "Latent heat does not cause a rise in temperature during a phase change because the heat energy is consumed in breaking intermolecular bonds.",
        "Common substances that undergo sublimation tested in exams include Ammonium Chloride, Camphor, Naphthalene, and Dry Ice (Solid CO2)."
